[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The two Mediterranean salmon breakfast wraps are positioned centrally on a warm, weathered oak wood surface, shot from a 3/4 overhead angle to showcase the texture of the tortillas and the vibrant contents. Each whole-wheat tortilla is tightly rolled, with the earthy, toasted brown color of the wheat bread providing a rustic contrast to the bright green baby spinach, pearly-pink flaked salmon, and translucent red onion slices peeking out from the ends. The wraps are placed side-by-side, one in focus and the other slightly blurred in the background, mirroring a meal for two. A generous portion of fresh, glistening mixed berries—blackberries, raspberries, and blueberries—is scattered casually on the side of each plate. The scene includes a small, crumpled linen napkin tucked beneath one edge of the plate and a few stray sprigs of fresh dill and a slice of lemon on the table surface. Soft, natural side light from a nearby window creates gentle shadows and highlights the moist, creamy texture of the hummus-salmon filling. The plates are simple, matte white ceramic. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating—lived-in, warm, authentic. Slight natural imperfections: a few berries have rolled away from the main pile, a small trace of fresh dill on the wood, and the wraps have a handmade, non-uniform shape. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. Warm, golden-hour color temperature—cozy and inviting. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from professional editorial food photography for a high-end cookbook."
]
